From c0477198745d939c0a988706f5eb9e83c83ebada Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 15:07:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kernel): wire the issue -> worktree -> work-folder
 linkage backbone

kernel_worktrees was schema-only (0 writes, always empty), so the kernel
stored none of the linkage and orientation guessed the active work-folder by
a filesystem heuristic ("most-complete folder wins") that breaks silently
under parallel features.

- forge worktree create <slug> [--issue <id>] [--work-folder <path>] now writes
  an idempotent kernel_worktrees row (keyed by absolute path) linking
  path/branch/issue_id/work_folder/git_common_dir, and drops a machine-readable
  .forge-issue marker in the work-folder.
- orientation.discoverWorkFolder + the new `forge worktree list` READ the
  linkage from the kernel (row work_folder, else issue_id -> marker scan),
  falling back to the folder heuristic only when no row exists.
- migration 007 adds nullable issue_id/work_folder columns (backward-compatible;
  a missing/un-migrated kernel degrades to the heuristic).
- driver gains registerWorktree/getWorktreeLinkage/listWorktrees (plain
  authority-table ops, not event-sourced).

RED-first test: test/commands/worktree-linkage.test.js. Regenerated the D20 bd
call-site artifact (orientation.js .beads line numbers shifted).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
